      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:5:36:1",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) الرَّجُلُ يُعْطَى الزَّكَاةَ يَقْسِمُهَا فِي أَصْحَابِهِ أَ يَأْخُذُ مِنْهَا شَيْئاً قَالَ نَعَمْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ali Bin Al Hakam, from Aban Bin Usman, from Saeed Bin Yasaar who said, ",
          "‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘The man is given the <span class=\"iTxt\">Zakāt</span> to distribute it among his companions. Can he take anything from it (for himself)?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Yes’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Ali ibn al-Hakam from Aban ibn ‘Uthman from Sa‘id ibn Yasar who has said the following: “I once asked abu ’Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man to whom Zakat is given for distribution, if he can take a certain amount for himself. He (the Imam) said, ‘Yes, can do so.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
